      "native_direct_technosphere_coordinates_match": true,
      "limitations": "Use the complete native Copper, at regional storage supply in place of a Latin-American primary-only refinery. The actual 3.6 global market supplies generic refined copper from primary, SX-EW, allocated co-product and recovered copper providers, all inspected with positive 1 kg copper references. The packaged 3.6-to-3.7 rename identifies this generic copper market with copper cathode, without a physical quantity change. Native regional storage includes primary/refined and secondary metal, concentrate supply/refining, freight and its original scrap input; retain that complete inventory once. This reuses the existing matching copper-consumer-supply decision after fresh inspection: the current 3.6 inventory SHA differs from the historical cathode-review row, so no equality with that older source inventory is asserted. Preserve signed kg at factor +1; do not add metal, separate concentrate refining, duplicate transport, a cathode-manufacturing process, recovery credit, ore/purity factor or new helper. Native historical German/RER consumption, technology, import and primary/secondary shares differ from the source global mix; allocation, background, delivery, biosphere and vintage differences remain warnings. Score effects are unquantified.",
